            <ArticleTitle>Young man with dyspnoea for 6 months; presenting with subacute tracheal obstruction due to leiomyoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-216096</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2016216096</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tracheal leiomyoma is a rare benign tumour with less than a 100 cases reported in the literature. We report a case of leiomyoma initially presenting and being treated as asthma until it lead to life-threatening tracheal obstruction, requiring immediate surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2016 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
